      "writtenOn": "2023-05-01T03:58:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should return a copy to avoid the caller modifying internal state by modifying contents of the array\n\nBut actually I remembered this guideline saying that APIs shouldn\u0027t use arrays in the first place: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/developers/docs/+/975a589941f728f6c6ce6fbbd7517ca854bc61ba/api-guidelines/index.md#methods-prefer-collection-over-array\n\nStill using an array would probably be OK if it was consistent with NsdServiceInfo, but actually NsdServiceInfo just uses String for the service type.\n\nTechnically the service type can\u0027t contain dots as per the RFC. So the problem is more about the hostname, which in theory could have labels containing dots.\n\nUsing a hostname with dots would probably be a horrible idea though... So maybe it\u0027s just simpler to use String and disallow labels with dots altogether ?",
      "revId": "c15ecf0305da955c84397afcfe8a891c03de816e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
